--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -4,12 +4,24 @@ A small team notes app. Next.js App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind.
 
 ## Status
 
-- Users live in `src/lib/users.ts` as an in-memory list.
-- `/dashboard` shows the current user and the team.
-- There is no sign-in, no billing, and no email yet.
+- Auth is [Better Auth](https://better-auth.com): email + password and Google sign-in.
+  Config in `src/lib/auth-options.ts`, API under `/api/auth/*`.
+- Users and sessions live in SQLite (`notely.db`, via Node's built-in `node:sqlite`).
+  Tables are created/updated automatically on server start (`src/instrumentation.ts`).
+- `src/lib/users.ts` reads users from the auth database; `getCurrentUser()` returns the
+  signed-in user, `requireUser()` redirects to `/sign-in` if there is none.
+- `/dashboard` is signed-in only (cookie check in `src/proxy.ts`, real session check in the page).
+- No email yet, so email verification and password reset are off. No billing.
 
 ## Develop
 
+Requires Node 22.13+.
+
 ```bash
+cp .env.example .env.local   # then set BETTER_AUTH_SECRET (openssl rand -base64 32)
 npm run dev
 ```
+
+Google sign-in is enabled only when `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` and `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` are set.
+Create an OAuth client in Google Cloud Console with the redirect URI
+`http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google`.
